2. Predict the Output – Data Object
#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;
int main() {
int x = 5;
int y = x;
x = 10;
printf(&quot;%d %d&quot;, x, y);
return 0;
}
Question: Predict the output and explain why changing x does not change y.

Data Object
Initially:
x = 5
y = x → y = 5
Then:
x = 10
y remains 5 because when y = x is executed, the value 5 is copied into y. Both are separate integer variables.
Output:
10 5
Why? x and y are separate data objects. Changing x later does not change y.
